details:
Some Externs have Ref variables as input, allowing the extern to modify multiple variables at once. Some of these externs do not properly modify the variable at all and even use the wrong value for the output noodles.
Example:
Vector3.SmoothDamp has a Vector3 ref variable, that when used in Udon does not update, but does in standard C#.
This function is used in Standard Assets's LookatTarget script. Since the ref variable does not work in Udon, using the same values set on the script version does not provide the same results.
Script example:

```
Vector3 angles = Vector3.zero;
Vector3 res = Vector3.SmoothDamp(Vector3.zero, new Vector3(100,100,100), ref angles, 0);
Debug.Log("S:Angles: " + angles);
Debug.Log("S:Res: " + res);
```

